# Canonical business logic

`lib/canonical/engine.ts` is the business-logic source for this app and for the iOS bundle `canonical-business.js`. `docs/CANONICAL_ARCHITECTURE.md` describes how web, iOS, and Firestore rules use it.

Before adding or changing a booking, warning, invoicing, labour, organisation, or date rule:

1. Search `lib/canonical` and call the existing function.
2. If the rule is new and both platforms must agree, add it under `lib/canonical/` (`engine.ts`, `warningRows.ts`, `warningSort.ts`, `timesheetSubmission.ts`, `timesheetPeriod.ts`, `organizationSettings.ts`, `billingAccess.ts`, `notificationPreferences.ts`, or `userRosterSegment.ts`), export it through `bundleEntry.ts`, and commit. Timesheet period identity, Awaiting / Signed off / Exported, sign-off / export write shape, and selectable historical payment runs are `timesheetPeriod.ts`. Organisation subscription access is `hasAccess` in `billingAccess.ts` — missing/none/pending/trialing/active open; past_due within 7 days of `lastPaymentFailedAt` open; canceled/unpaid/paused/incomplete and expired past_due closed. Do not invent a second status enum. The pre-commit hook packs the script and refuses the commit when the iOS checkout has an uncommitted packed file. Warning row identity for qualifications, unverified operatives, and unbooked labour is `warningRows.ts`. Ordering already-computed warning rows by coverage day is `warningSort.ts`. Timesheet submit deadline, notify-at, and notice copy are `timesheetSubmission.ts`. The organisation material cut-off clock is `parseMaterialCutOff` / `resolveMaterialCutOffClock` in `organizationSettings.ts` — never `users/{uid}.notificationPreferences.materialCutOffHour`. User-level notification toggles, inbox destination kinds, device-push allow-list (`devicePushNotificationTypes`, `notificationDeliversDevicePush`), and unread badge (`unreadNotificationBadgeCount`) are `notificationPreferences.ts`. Active / Inactive / Pending on people lists is `userRosterSegment.ts` (`rosterSegment`, `listedRosterUsers`) — an anonymised deleted profile is Inactive; a leftover invite whose `userEmails` claim is gone is not a live pending row. Session company choice (`chooseSessionOrganization`, `orgAccessProbeFromReads`, `sessionMembershipIds`) is in `engine.ts` and must be packed so iOS does not keep a second picker. `sessionMembershipIds` always keeps remembered / user-document / explicit companies. Company name writes are `organizationNameWriteFields` — never persist `name: ''`.
3. Use `adoptCurrentOrganization` and `organizationContextStillCurrent` for organisation-scoped async work. Cache and persistence keys include the organisation id.
4. If web and iOS disagree, trace the first divergence. Do not change a screen so its number matches the other platform.
5. Add a regression test in `lib/canonical/canonical.test.ts`.
6. Update `docs/CANONICAL_ARCHITECTURE.md` when the boundary changes.

Screens, navigation, and copy stay in the app. The iOS parity rule for nested screens still applies to UI work. It does not mean copying a business calculation into a component.

Operational or shared-rule work: follow `.cursor/rules/shared-operational-change.mdc` and emit its follow-on prompt for the other platform.
